        "mission_intent": "We need a fully developed continuous monitoring specification for our enterprise environment that aligns with NIST SP 800-137 guidance. The spec should establish tiered monitoring frequencies based on system impact levels\u2014high-impact systems monitored most frequently, moderate next, and low-impact least frequently\u2014with specific cadences defined for each tier. It must also account for control volatility: highly volatile technical controls like configuration management and hardware/software inventory should be assessed more often, ideally using automated SCAP-validated tools that provide on-demand alerting and status, while relatively static controls such as personnel security items like position categorization and personnel screening can follow a less frequent assessment cycle. The specification needs to identify and prioritize security controls and assessment objects that support critical security functions\u2014think firewalls, log management servers, and similar infrastructure\u2014flagging them for elevated monitoring frequency consistent with our business impact analysis. Please include the data sources each monitoring activity will draw from, reporting rollup procedures from system level to organizational dashboards, and the roles responsible for reviewing and acting on findings. We'd like a draft ready for CISO review by the end of next month so we can begin phased implementation in the following quarter.",
